Phase 2 of the Growth build-out. The worker can now authorise Google accounts,
pull real data into the growth_* tables, and tell you exactly what is missing
before anyone debugs the UI.

New: worker/src/modules/growth/
  googleAuth.ts  OAuth consent/exchange/refresh. Dependency-free (googleapis is
                 huge; this needs three calls and Node 22 has fetch). State is
                 HMAC-signed with the service-role key so a forged callback
                 cannot attach an attacker's Google account to another tenant.
                 access_type=offline + prompt=consent because Google omits the
                 refresh_token on repeat authorisation otherwise, which breaks
                 background sync a week later rather than immediately.
  store.ts       The only place growth_provider_secrets is touched. Refresh
                 tokens are never overwritten with null on re-auth. Access
                 tokens refresh inside a 2-minute skew window.
  providers.ts   Search Console (paged searchAnalytics, window ends at T-2
                 because GSC data lags ~2 days and earlier rows keep changing),
                 PageSpeed Insights (Core Web Vitals -> derived issue list),
                 Business Profile (locations, completeness scoring, reviews,
                 reply write-back).
  routes.ts      /api/growth: connect, callback, sync/search-console,
                 sync/seo-audit, sync/business-profile, reviews/:id/publish,
                 plus setup/status and setup/schema self-checks.

Provider availability, verified against Google's docs 2026-08-17:
  Search Console and PageSpeed need only an enabled API — usable immediately.
  Business Profile REQUIRES an approved access request (verified profile owned
  60+ days). Until approved the quota is 0 QPM and every call 403s. The code is
  complete; sync failures matching /403|quota|permission/ append that
  explanation so the error is not mistaken for a bug.

Two issues found by testing rather than review:
  - A failed 'pending' bookkeeping write blocked OAuth from starting at all.
    That write is not authoritative (the callback upserts) so it is now logged
    and non-fatal.
  - upsertRows' Record<string, unknown>[] signature rejected typed row arrays;
    widened to readonly object[].

Tests (7 pass): state round-trip, forged-tenant rejection, wrong-key rejection,
malformed input, consent-URL parameters incl. asserting the client secret never
appears in a browser-bound URL, listing completeness scoring, and review mapping
(low ratings flag rather than silently queue; unknown star strings do not crash
a sync). Worker test script now discovers all module tests, not just marketing-ai.

Live smoke-tested against the real runtime: setup/status reports ready with all
env present and lists exactly what is missing without, unsupported providers
400, forged state 400, and the generated consent URL carries offline access,
consent prompt, correct scope, signed state, and no client secret.

Frontend build, typecheck, and all 10 guard tests remain green.

Setup still required by Ned (cannot be done from code): create the OAuth client
and enable APIs in Google Cloud, submit the Business Profile access request, set
GOOGLE_OAUTH_*/PAGESPEED_API_KEY on Railway, and apply the growth migration to
Supabase. /api/growth/setup/status and /setup/schema verify each of those.

